+### Duration
+
+The {class}`Duration` type converts a length of time into a
+{class}`datetime.timedelta`. A value is either a whole number of seconds, like
+`120`, or one or more number and unit groups, like `1h30m`. The units are `d`
+(days), `h` (hours), `m` (minutes), and `s` (seconds). Each unit may be used
+at most once, and units must appear in that order. Units are case-insensitive,
+and spaces are not allowed.
+
+```{eval-rst}
+.. click:example::
+
+    @click.command()
+    @click.option("--timeout", type=click.Duration(), default="30s")
+    def wait(timeout):
+        click.echo(f"Waiting {timeout.total_seconds():g} seconds")
+
+.. click:run::
+
+    invoke(wait, args=["--timeout=1h30m"])
+    invoke(wait, args=["--timeout=90"])
+    invoke(wait, args=["--timeout=1.5h"])
+    invoke(wait, args=["--help"])
+```
+
